WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:10.180
Cohen injected newborn mice every day with a crude extract of male mouse salivary

2
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:15.380
gland. A crude extract is a mixture, not a single purified protein.

3
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.340
He expected a particular result.

4
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.260
The sympathetic ganglia should be enlarged.

5
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.020
And they were.

6
00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:26.563
But the mice did something else as well.

7
00:00:27.423 --> 00:00:31.023
They opened their eyelids about seven days after birth.

8
00:00:31.843 --> 00:00:34.523
The usual age is 12 to 14 days.

9
00:00:35.523 --> 00:00:37.563
Their teeth also came through early.

10
00:00:38.343 --> 00:00:41.643
That did not fit. Neither of these was expected.

11
00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:47.637
Purified nerve growth factor, given alone, did none of that.

12
00:00:48.157 --> 00:00:53.357
So the crude extract must have carried a second protein, with its own activity.

13
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:58.817
This one acts on skin, so it was named epidermal growth factor.

14
00:00:59.657 --> 00:01:03.337
One extract, two proteins, two activities.

15
00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:08.790
The halo assay counted nerve fibers, and only nerve fibers.

16
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:14.390
It could not show eyelids or teeth, so it was blind to epidermal growth factor.

17
00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:19.250
A whole newborn mouse responds to everything in a crude extract.

18
00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:25.450
When you start from a mixture, the assay you choose decides which molecule you find.
